7,Kiwai language,https://grokipedia.com/page/kiwai_language,"Northeastern Kiwai refers to a cluster of closely related dialects within the Kiwai language family, spoken primarily in the Gulf Province of Papua New Guinea. These dialects exhibit a high degree of mutual intelligibility among speakers...","Kiwai, Northeast",Trans-New Guinea
8,Northeast Kiwai,https://lingweb.eva.mpg.de/channumerals/Kiwai-Northeast.htm,"Other comments: Northeast Kiwai is spoken by about 6,000 speakers in Gulf province, Papua New Guinae. The Kope dialect of Northeast Kiwai has a 2-cycle system with morphemes for 'hand' and 'foot' up to 20 and continue counting up to 100.","Kiwai, Northeast",Trans-New Guinea
